{"name":"Footie Pyjamas","hex":"#e6cee6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"footie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of footy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blanket sleeper or similar covering that covers the foot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/footie"},{"term":"pyjamas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["UK standard form of pajamas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pyjamas"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blanket sleeper","blocks":[{"text":"The blanket sleeper is a type of especially warm sleeper or footie pajama worn primarily during the winter in the United States and Canada. The garment is worn especially by young children."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/American_sleepers1.jpg/330px-American_sleepers1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanket_sleeper"},{"title":"Pajamas","blocks":[{"text":"Pajamas or pyjamas, sometimes colloquially shortened to PJs, jammies, jim-jams, or in South Asia, night suits, are several related types of clothing worn as nightwear or while lounging. Pajamas are soft garments derived from the Indian and Iranian bottom-wear, the pyjamas, which were adopted in the Western world as nightwear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Muslim_girl_india1844_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Muslim_girl_india1844_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pajamas"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Two_piece_pajamas.jpg/250px-Two_piece_pajamas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Two_piece_pajamas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thum